  abstract = {The fast cyber threats' evolution, particularly AI-Powered attacks, necessitated advanced defense strategies based on artificial intelligence, machine learning and deep learning. Our survey synthesizes some studies and reviews which treated and classify AI-Powered and AI-Driven cyber attacks in recent years, including AI-Driven social engineering attacks, deepfakes, ransomware attacks, etc. This classification provides a comprehensive overview of AI's power to improve cyber security in different contexts. We highlight also the work carried out in some papers which presented some AI based solutions against these attacks, such as Multi-factor authentication (MFA), training employees to check information before sharing or posting it, using strong passwords, etc. Therefore, we conclude that there is an urgent need for resilient cybersecurity frameworks to protect digital infrastructures in an increasingly adversarial landscape. In summary, this study highlights the dual role of AI as both a threat tool and a defense tool. \copyright{} 2025 IEEE.},
